Given in the Cartesian coordinate system $xOy$, the parametric equation of the conic curve $C$ is $\begin{cases} x=2\cos \theta \\ y=\sin \theta\end{cases}$ (where $\theta$ is the parameter), and the fixed point $A(0, -\sqrt{3})$, $F_{1}$, $F_{2}$ are the left and right foci of the conic curve $C$, respectively. The line $l$ passes through point $A$ and $F_{1}$.  
